From 849b69978685febf9317f441da0317a20038aa54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:07:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/69] CUDA/HIP: GDN fused SSM_CONV and alpha/beta projections
 in one grid (GGML_HIP_GDN_CONV_AB)

The fused conv (ssm_conv_fused_f32, d_conv 4, +SILU) and the alpha/beta MMVQ (mul_mat_vec_q_gdn_ab) of a GDN layer
are independent (qkv product vs. the layer input). The SSM_CONV handler now looks past the views and the nodes the
GDN prologue elides; when the alpha/beta pattern follows, gdn_conv_ab<type, n_tokens> runs both: blocks
[0, nr/128) are the conv's blocks, the rest the (head, projection) blocks, through shared block bodies
(ssm_conv_fused_f32_block in ssm-conv.cuh, mul_mat_vec_q_gdn_ab_block) - same per-block code, bitwise equal.
Skipped when the alpha/beta outputs share memory with the conv's input or output. Types Q8_0/Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K.

rocprofv3 (Qwen3.8-27B, MTP n=4, verify): conv 4.68 us + alpha/beta 4.90 us + one boundary -> 5.54 us, 48 per
verify (-48 kernels). Greedy md5 (plain and MTP) equal to 9f83f1f81. test-backend-ops SSM_CONV 45/45,
GATED_DELTA_NET 36/36.
